      \field{abstract}{Laminar natural convection in a fluid-filled cylinder with different end wall temperatures is investigated in a three-dimensional numerical study and is experimentally verified. The influences of fluid and geometrical parameters, like Rayleigh number (Ra {<} 8 x 104), Prandtl number (0.023 {<} Pr {<} 135), aspect ratio height/diameter (0.5 {<} H/D {<} 2), and inclination angle (0” {<} {CY}{<} 180”) on convective motion and heat transfer are presented. Maximum heat transfer and greatest velocities are found for H/D = 1 at inclination angles of c1z 45”-60”.}
